  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced capacity of the government and social partners to develop a national labour policy, and mainstream SDGs relating to employment and DW into national development and crisis response frameworks</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under ENABLE, the ILO is planning to support the Central Administration of Statistics( CAS) in undertaking a new follow-up labour force and household living conditions survey. 
The survey will be telephone-based, covering the whole of Lebanon. Exact dates are to be agreed upon and confirmed with CAS. 
The ILO&apos;s efforts to develop a national employment policy (NEP) for Lebanon are awaiting political commitments. An Employment Diagnostic has been prepared and, if political conditions improve during this biennium, work can restart with the nomination of an inter-ministerial tripartite commission to draft the NEP with technical assistance from the ILO.</narrative>
  </description>
